/*
 * Swap maps, for board sizes 1 to 27.
 *
 * swapMaps[size][row][col] = win rate of first player (red, top-bottom)
 * after playing this cell as first move on an empty board, without swap.
 * 0: weak first move, do not swap. 1: strong first move, swap.
 * row 0 is top row ("1"), col 0 is left column ("a").
 *
 * Can be used by an AI to decide whether to swap opponent first move,
 * or to choose a balanced first move (value close to 0.5).
 *
 * How these values were computed:
 *
 * - Sizes 1 to 4: exact solution, by minimax solver (1: winning, 0: losing).
 *   Katahex does not support boards smaller than 4x4.
 *
 * - Sizes 5 to 27: katahex (KataGo v1.12.4 fork), model hex27x3-b18c384n2-s658497536-d2995073,
 *   on a NVIDIA RTX A1000 Laptop GPU, 16 search threads.
 *   For each cell, on an empty board, with these GTP commands:
 *
 *       boardsize <size>
 *       kata-time_settings none
 *       kata-set-param maxPlayouts 1000
 *       clear_board
 *       play black <cell>
 *       kata-genmove_analyze white maxmoves 1
 *
 *   Value = 1 - winrate of white best move.
 *   Config overrides: searchFactorWhenWinning=1.0 (else search is cut short in unbalanced positions),
 *   ponderingEnabled=false.
 *   "set_position" is not used because it always sets black to play.
 *   Only half of cells are searched: value of (row, col) is copied to (size-1-row, size-1-col)
 *   by 180° rotation symmetry.
 *   Precision: compared to 10000 playouts on some 14x14 cells, values differ by about 0.02.
 *
 * Model is trained up to 27x27, so larger boards are not computed.
 */
